## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design data minimization, policy grounding, and auditable RBAC in a multi-tenant environment using Azure OpenAI; it tests integration points and test strategy.

## Key Concepts
- guided prompt design
- per-tenant RBAC with Azure AD
- Cognitive Search KB grounding
- immutable Data Lake logs
- deterministic runbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
async function boundaryDecision(user, request) {
  const ctx = await getTenantContext(user.tenantId); // from Azure AD
  const policy = await queryKB("policy", ctx);
  const subset = applyMinimization(request.data, policy, ctx);
  // force RBAC at data layer
  if (!hasAccess(user, subset)) throw new Error("Access denied");
  const rationale = `Selected ${subset.length} records for tenant ${ctx.name} per policy.`;
  await logAudit({user, request, subset, ctx});
  return { subset, rationale };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test data minimization guarantees end-to-end? 
- How do you handle policy KB drift and versioning? 
- What latency budgets and retries would you enforce for OpenAI calls?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a compliant, production-grade retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) assistant for contract processing. It evaluates understanding of multi-tenant security, data isolation, and regulatory compliance patterns.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) with Cognitive Search knowledge base
- Per-tenant isolation via Key Vault and customer-managed keys (CMK)
- PII redaction with consent-based access control
- Policy engine to detect and block sensitive prompt patterns
- End-to-end audit trail to Data Lake for compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode policy snippet
function isAllowed(prompt, piiPresent, consentGiven) {
  if (piiPresent && !consentGiven) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'PII detected without consent' };
  }
  if (containsSensitivePatterns(prompt)) {
    return { allowed: false, reason: 'Sensitive content blocked' };
  }
  return { allowed: true };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests knowledge of Azure OpenAI integration, policy-based gating, and tenant isolation in a practical chat app.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-policy retrieval from Azure Key Vault
- Input screening with Azure Text Analytics
- Policy gating before Azure OpenAI calls
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and KB in Blob
- Per-tenant auditing to Data Lake

